From 4167cfb012970b5bd3204d4c4100616ffee08748 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:07:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Android: offer the phone's text-to-speech to the table as
 window.odmSpeech

The mirror of the dictation bridge. SpeechPlugin wraps Android's
TextToSpeech (media stream, the engine's installed voices, rate, pitch,
volume) and speaks a passage as one take of chunks, answering when the
last one is spoken or when stop() or a newer take cuts it short.
speech-core.ts splits long passages under the engine's input limit,
names the voices, and installs window.odmSpeech only when the phone has
a working engine. The server's screens read passages with it where the
server has no narration, or when the player asks for the phone's voice
(server src/lib/native-speech.ts). The manifest declares the
TTS_SERVICE query, without which Android 11+ never connects the engine.

